# LeviOS

A 16-bit x86 operating system written in Assembly.

## Prerequisites

- **NASM:** Must be installed and available on your PATH.
  - **Windows:** Download from [nasm.us](https://www.nasm.us/) or `winget install nasm`
  - **Linux:** `sudo apt install nasm`
- **QEMU:** Required for running the OS natively.
  - **Windows:** Default install path (`C:\Program Files\qemu\`)
  - **Linux:** System PATH (`sudo apt install qemu-system-x86 qemu-utils`)
- **Terminal / Shell:**
  - **Windows:** Git Bash
  - **Linux:** Standard Terminal

*(Note: Linux package installation commands above are for Debian/Ubuntu-based distros; adapt `apt install`/`pacman -S`/etc. to your distro's package manager if using Arch, Fedora, etc.)*

## Running the OS

Run all commands from inside the `LeviOS` project root directory.

### 1. Build & Run in QEMU (Native)
Assembles all programs, generates `build/disk.img`, and launches the OS in QEMU:

make
make run